        "title": "Study 1 — Significant at four weeks",
        "show_image_mobile": true,
        "background_heading": "Study Background",
        "background_text": "28 people with low mood were randomly split: 13 took 12 g of inositol daily, 15 took a placebo, for four weeks — and nobody knew who had which. The reason researchers tried it at all: inositol levels in spinal fluid had been found lower than normal in this group (Levine et al., 1995).†",
        "attributes_heading": "Study Attributes",
